AB  - In this paper, we consider a viral dynamical model with the wild-type virus and mutant. The threshold determining its dynamical behavior is found. When the threshold is less than one, the virus will be extinct ultimately; when it is greater than one, the model has a unique positive equilibrium which is locally asymptotically stable, and within-host virus will persist.
