AB  - In this paper, we investigate the global dynamics for a nonlocal dispersal SIV epidemic model with vaccinations and latent delays. The well-posedness of the solutions including the existence and uniqueness, the nonnegativity and boundedness of solutions are obtained. The basic reproduction numbers R-1 and R-2 with respect to strain 1 and 2 are calculated by using the next generation matrix method, and the existence of equilibria is further acquired. The threshold criteria on the global stability of equilibria are established by constructing suitable Lyapunov functionals and using the LaSalle's invariant principle. The main results show that the two vaccinations not only can have effects on the stability of the single-strain infection equilibria, but can also allow the existence of the coexistence equilibrium. Moreover, the numerical examples are presented to illustrate the main theoretical results.
